 ## Fuzzing
 
-`ANYPS5_BUILD_FUZZERS` builds `relinker_conversion_fuzzer`, a libFuzzer target that runs the whole conversion on its input, as the web converter does. It requires `ANYPS5_RELINKER_ONLY`, Clang on Linux and the compiler-rt sanitizer runtimes (`libclang-rt-18-dev` on Ubuntu 24.04). Every target is built with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, without `-fsanitize=function`: that check reads a signature before the target of every indirect call and faults on the generated code the codegen tests call. The first input byte selects the target system (modulo 3: Linux, Windows, macOS), bit 2 `--to-intel` and the byte shifted right by 3, modulo 3, the `unused-filter` level; the remaining bytes are the executable. A conversion that throws a `std::exception` is a rejected input; a sanitizer report, an abort or a timeout is a finding.
+`ANYPS5_BUILD_FUZZERS` builds `relinker_conversion_fuzzer`, a libFuzzer target that runs the whole conversion on its input, as the web converter does. It requires `ANYPS5_RELINKER_ONLY`, Clang on Linux and the compiler-rt sanitizer runtimes (`libclang-rt-18-dev` on Ubuntu 24.04). Every target is built with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, without `-fsanitize=function`: that check reads a signature before the target of every indirect call and faults on the generated code the codegen tests call. The first input byte selects the target system (modulo 3: Linux, Windows, macOS), bit 2 `--to-intel` and the byte shifted right by 3, modulo 3, the `unused-filter` level. When the byte shifted right by 3 is less than 3, the remaining bytes are the executable. Otherwise the next two bytes, little-endian, select further options and the executable follows them: bit 0 `--to-rosetta`, 1 `--to-avx`, 2 `--frame-red-zone`, 3 `--lazy-binding`, 4 `--skip-syscall-check`, 5 `--trap-sdk-syscall-stubs`, 6 `--function-symbol-roots`, 7 `--omit-unavailable-dependencies`, 8 `--windows-gui`, 9 `--trace-imports`, 10 `--windows-diagnostics` and 11 the target system's fixed base, whose address bits 12 to 15 select. An option the command line refuses with the selected target or with another selected option is dropped, as `core/relinker/fuzz/FuzzOptions.hpp` decodes it; `--to-rosetta` and `--to-avx` turn on `--to-intel`, and the web converter's Windows conversions are the Windows target with bit 10. `relinker_fuzz_options` checks that every decoded configuration passes the conversion's option checks. A conversion that throws a `std::exception` is a rejected input; a sanitizer report, an abort or a timeout is a finding.
 
 ```sh
 cmake -S . -B build-fuzz -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DANYPS5_RELINKER_ONLY=ON -DANYPS5_BUILD_FUZZERS=ON -DBUILD_TESTING=ON -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++
 cmake --build build-fuzz --target relinker_conversion_fuzzer
-python3 tools/relinker_fuzz_seeds.py build-fuzz/fuzz-corpus
+python3 tools/relinker_fuzz_seeds.py build-fuzz/fuzz-corpus --extended-options
 build-fuzz/tests/relinker_conversion_fuzzer build-fuzz/fuzz-corpus -fork=2 -max_total_time=1200 -timeout=20
 ```
 
-`relinker_fuzz_seeds.py` writes the executables built by the relinker's Python tests as seeds, one per target system. With `BUILD_TESTING=ON`, CTest runs 20000 inputs from an empty corpus as `relinker_conversion_fuzzer`. Findings are written to the working directory as `crash-*`, `timeout-*` or `oom-*`; reproduce one with `build-fuzz/tests/relinker_conversion_fuzzer <file>`.
+`relinker_fuzz_seeds.py` writes the executables built by the relinker's Python tests as seeds, one per target system; `--extended-options` adds one seed per target system and further option. With `BUILD_TESTING=ON`, CTest runs 20000 inputs from an empty corpus as `relinker_conversion_fuzzer`. Findings are written to the working directory as `crash-*`, `timeout-*` or `oom-*`; reproduce one with `build-fuzz/tests/relinker_conversion_fuzzer <file>`.
 
 `tools/relinker_seed_manifest.py <corpus>` describes each file of a flat fuzz corpus as one JSON object: its name, its size, the SHA-256 of its content and its first byte, which selects the target system.
 
